General qualifications:<br>
Motivated, self-starter;
Have to possess strong writing skills;
Excellent communication skills;
BA degree;
High attention to detail/strong follow-up skills;
Needs to demonstrate a proven ability to work collaboratively as well as independently;
Should be eager to learn and grow in the position;
Ability to accept and apply constructive feedback;
Flexibility;
Punctuality/ respect for deadlines;
Self-discipline and strong work ethic;
Ought to possess an ability to multitask in a busy work environment while maintaining strong attention to detail;
Must be highly organized and able to consistently follow project organizational deadlines.

Requirements specific to the position:<br>
An inherent understanding of storytelling and dramatic structure;
Must be able at times to work independently and in collaboration with printers, publishers and assistant editors;
Needs to have at least one year professional experience with inEffects, inPrinting, and inPremiere;
Experience with learning management systems, a plus;
Comfortable with different operating systems;
Interest in learning new software and staying current with technological changes in the industry;
Willingness to occasionally work long hours and on weekends in order to meet delivery deadlines;
Willingness to proofread and make changes as many times as necessary.<br><br>
Primary duties and responsibilities include:<br>
Editing long form and short form projects, both working independently and with an editor, depending on the project;
Preparing project elements for use in publishing;
Preparing outputs and deliverables;
Screening of quality control materials;
Preparing text for transcription;
Managing text archive.
